{% comment %}
  Dial - a drawn face, where the minutes are a swept wedge rather than a hand.

  This is the design the whole extension is arranged around. A minute hand
  points at one minute; the picture it is drawn in will hang on the wall for
  fifteen. So there is no minute hand. There is a wedge that starts at the
  minute this was drawn and sweeps as far as the clock will have moved by the
  time the device next asks - `dither.window_minutes`, which is the device's
  own refresh rate rather than a number guessed here.

  Read it as "somewhere in there", and it is never wrong. Read a minute hand
  the same way and it is wrong fourteen minutes in fifteen, while looking
  precise about it, which is worse.

  The hour hand is drawn exactly, because it moves seven and a half degrees in
  a quarter of an hour and nobody can see that.

  Everything is a rotation about the centre, so there is no trigonometry in a
  templating language that has none: the arc is a dashed circle turned to
  start where it should, which is the same trick a donut chart uses.
{% endcomment %}

{%- assign shift = 0 -%}
{%- if extension.values.utc_offset_hours != blank -%}
  {%- assign shift = extension.values.utc_offset_hours | times: 3600 | minus: dither.offset_seconds -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign stamp = "now" | date: "%s" | plus: shift -%}

{%- assign hour24 = stamp | date: "%H" | times: 1 -%}
{%- assign minute = stamp | date: "%M" | times: 1 -%}
{%- assign hour = hour24 | modulo: 12 -%}

{%- assign mins = hour24 | times: 60 | plus: minute -%}

{%- assign window_minutes = dither.window_minutes | at_least: 1 -%}
{%- assign window = window_minutes | at_most: 60 -%}
{%- if extension.values.show_window == false %}{% assign window = 0 %}{% endif -%}

{%- comment %} Where the hands are put, and why it is not where the clock
  says.

  This drawing goes up now and stays up until the device next wakes. A hand at
  the minute of drawing is right for an instant and then falls behind for the
  whole window - by the end it is a quarter of an hour slow, every time. Put it
  at the *middle* of the window instead and it is half a window fast to begin
  with and half a window slow at the end: the same error, but split either side
  of the truth, so the average miss is halved and the hand sweeps through the
  right time rather than trailing it.

  The wedge still starts where the clock actually is, so the pair reads
  correctly: the span is where the time will be, the hand is the middle of it.

  A filter cannot appear inside an `if`, so every step is assigned first.
{% endcomment -%}
{%- assign lead = window_minutes | divided_by: 2 -%}
{%- assign mid = minute | plus: lead -%}
{%- assign half = mid | divided_by: 2 -%}
{%- assign hour_angle = hour | times: 30 | plus: half -%}
{%- assign minute_angle = minute | times: 6 -%}
{%- assign hand_angle = mid | times: 6 -%}


{%- comment %} The dial is square, so it is fitted to the shorter side, and
  the room left over decides whether anything is written under it. {% endcomment -%}
{%- assign box_w = shape.width | at_least: 120 -%}
{%- assign box_h = shape.height | at_least: 120 -%}
{%- assign pad = box_w | divided_by: 22 | at_least: 8 | at_most: 20 -%}

{%- assign caption = "" -%}
{%- if extension.values.heading != blank %}{% assign caption = extension.values.heading %}{% endif -%}

{%- comment %} A face is square and a band is not, so in a wide box the dial
  stands beside what it would otherwise have written underneath. Centred alone
  in a twelve-by-four band it is a small clock in a lot of paper; beside the
  date and the sentence it is a band that reads. {% endcomment -%}
{%- assign wide_at = box_h | times: 16 | divided_by: 10 -%}
{%- assign beside = false -%}
{%- if box_w > wide_at and box_w > 380 %}{% assign beside = true %}{% endif -%}

{%- assign said_text = mins | time_in_words: window_minutes -%}

{%- assign under = 0 -%}
{%- if notices.size > 0 %}{% assign under = 34 %}{% endif -%}
{%- assign dated = false -%}

{%- if beside -%}
  {%- assign room_h = box_h | minus: under | minus: pad | minus: pad -%}
  {%- comment %} Never more than half the width, or the words beside it have
    nowhere to go. {% endcomment -%}
  {%- assign by_width = box_w | times: 46 | divided_by: 100 -%}
  {%- assign side = room_h | at_most: by_width | at_least: 90 -%}
  {%- if extension.values.show_date != false %}{% assign dated = true %}{% endif -%}
  {%- comment %} The sentence takes the width the face left over, up to the
    point where it would start competing with the face for attention. {% endcomment -%}
  {%- assign said_chars = said_text | size | at_least: 10 -%}
  {%- assign spare_w = box_w | minus: side | minus: pad | minus: pad | minus: pad -%}
  {%- assign by_chars = spare_w | times: 100 | divided_by: said_chars | divided_by: 50 -%}
  {%- assign said_size = side | divided_by: 3 | at_most: by_chars | at_most: 54 | at_least: 15 -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- if caption != "" %}{% assign under = under | plus: 30 %}{% endif -%}
  {%- if extension.values.show_date != false and box_h > 260 %}{% assign dated = true %}{% endif -%}
  {%- comment %} The line plus its gap plus the descenders of "Thursday",
    which is what the first attempt forgot. {% endcomment -%}
  {%- if dated %}{% assign under = under | plus: 46 %}{% endif -%}
  {%- assign room_h = box_h | minus: under | minus: pad | minus: pad -%}
  {%- assign room_w = box_w | minus: pad | minus: pad -%}
  {%- assign side = room_w | at_most: room_h | at_least: 90 -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- assign said = said_text -%}

{%- comment %} Numerals need pixels to be legible. At the small end of this
  design's range the face is 150 pixels across, where a numeral is six points
  and a smudge, so it is drawn as ticks alone whatever the setting says. {% endcomment -%}
{%- assign numerals = extension.values.numerals | default: "quarters" -%}
{%- if side < 170 %}{% assign numerals = "none" %}{% endif -%}
{%- if side < 260 and numerals == "all" %}{% assign numerals = "quarters" %}{% endif -%}

{%- comment %} The wedge is a dashed circle: as much of its circumference as
  the window is of an hour, turned to begin at the minute hand. The radius is
  78, so the circumference is 490. {% endcomment -%}
{%- assign sweep = window | times: 490 | divided_by: 60 -%}
{%- assign sweep_from = minute_angle | minus: 90 -%}

<div class="screen">
  <div class="content layout layout--{% if beside %}row{% else %}col{% endif %} layout--center"
       style="gap: {{ pad }}px; padding: {{ pad }}px">
    {% if caption != "" and beside == false %}
      <p class="t-bold t-upper t-center truncate" style="font-size: {{ side | divided_by: 18 | at_least: 11 | at_most: 18 }}px; width: 100%">
        {{ caption }}
      </p>
    {% endif %}

    <svg viewBox="0 0 200 200" width="{{ side }}" height="{{ side }}"
         fill="none" stroke="black" style="flex: none">
      <circle cx="100" cy="100" r="95" stroke-width="4"/>

      {%- comment %} Every fifth mark is heavier: a face is read by the hour
        first and the rest is texture. {% endcomment -%}
      {% for tick in (0..59) %}
        {%- assign fifth = tick | modulo: 5 -%}
        {%- assign quarter = tick | modulo: 15 -%}
        {% if fifth == 0 or side > 220 %}
          <line x1="100" y1="12" x2="100"
                y2="{% if quarter == 0 %}30{% elsif fifth == 0 %}25{% else %}18{% endif %}"
                stroke-width="{% if quarter == 0 %}6{% elsif fifth == 0 %}3.5{% else %}1.5{% endif %}"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                transform="rotate({{ tick | times: 6 }} 100 100)"/>
        {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}

      {% if numerals != "none" %}
        {% for mark in (1..12) %}
          {%- assign angle = mark | times: 30 -%}
          {%- assign quarter = mark | modulo: 3 -%}
          {% if numerals == "all" or quarter == 0 %}
            {%- comment %} Turned into place, then turned back, so the numeral
              stands upright wherever it lands. {% endcomment -%}
            <g transform="rotate({{ angle }} 100 100)">
              <g transform="rotate({{ 0 | minus: angle }} 100 46)">
                <text x="100" y="46" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="middle"
                      fill="black" stroke="none"
                      font-family="Inter, sans-serif" font-weight="700"
                      font-size="{% if numerals == 'all' %}17{% else %}21{% endif %}">{{ mark }}</text>
              </g>
            </g>
          {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
      {% endif %}

      {% if window > 0 %}
        {%- comment %} The span this drawing is claiming. Hatching would
          disappear at this width on a 1-bit panel, so it is an outlined band:
          two thin arcs and the fill between them left as paper. {% endcomment -%}
        <circle cx="100" cy="100" r="78" stroke-width="17" stroke="black"
                stroke-dasharray="{{ sweep }} 490" opacity="1"
                transform="rotate({{ sweep_from }} 100 100)"/>
        <circle cx="100" cy="100" r="78" stroke-width="13" stroke="white"
                stroke-dasharray="{{ sweep }} 490"
                transform="rotate({{ sweep_from }} 100 100)"/>
      {% endif %}

      {%- comment %} The minute hand marks where the window *starts*. It is the
        one thing here that is exactly true at the moment of drawing. {% endcomment -%}
      {%- comment %} The minute hand, in the middle of the span rather than at
        the start of it. {% endcomment -%}
      <line x1="100" y1="104" x2="100" y2="34" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round"
            transform="rotate({{ hand_angle }} 100 100)"/>
      <line x1="100" y1="106" x2="100" y2="56" stroke-width="9" stroke-linecap="round"
            transform="rotate({{ hour_angle }} 100 100)"/>
      <circle cx="100" cy="100" r="7" fill="black" stroke="none"/>
      <circle cx="100" cy="100" r="2.5" fill="white" stroke="none"/>
    </svg>

    {% if beside %}
      {%- comment %} What the face cannot say precisely, said in words - and
        the date, which is the other question a clock on a wall gets asked. {% endcomment -%}
      <div class="stack fit" style="justify-content: center; gap: 6px; min-width: 0">
        {% if caption != "" %}
          <p class="t-bold t-upper truncate" style="font-size: {{ side | divided_by: 14 | at_least: 11 | at_most: 16 }}px">{{ caption }}</p>
        {% endif %}
        <p class="t-bold clamp-2" style="font-size: {{ said_size }}px; line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -0.02em">
          {{ said }}
        </p>
        {% if dated %}
          <p class="truncate" style="font-size: {{ said_size | divided_by: 2 | at_least: 12 | at_most: 22 }}px">
            {{ stamp | date: "%A %-d %B" }}
          </p>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    {% elsif dated %}
      <p class="t-center truncate" style="font-size: {{ side | divided_by: 16 | at_least: 12 | at_most: 20 }}px; width: 100%">
        {{ stamp | date: "%A %-d %B" }}
      </p>
    {% endif %}
  </div>

  {% comment %}
    Where another extension gets to say something on this screen.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% if notices.size > 0 %}
    <div class="notice-strip" style="padding: 6px {{ pad }}px">
      {% for notice in notices %}
        {% if notice.overflow %}
          <span class="notice notice--more">+{{ notice.overflow }}</span>
        {% else %}
          <span class="notice notice--{{ notice.level }}" title="{{ notice.text }}">
            <span class="i i-{{ notice.icon }}"></span>
          </span>
        {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}

      {% if shape.wide and notices[0].text != blank %}
        <span class="notice-said">{{ notices[0].text }}</span>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  {% endif %}
</div>
